<!--Post: 9785--><!--Time: 1109638484-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9785"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know that the immediate family of Dennis Rader is suffering............BUT the families of the victims have been suffering for decades and deep down inside, I am just not ready to dwell too much on how Dennis Rader&#39;s family is suffering, especially when I see the victims families and see the pain and anguish that they have had to live with all these years.  I will confess I feel some sympathy for his children, but I just don&#39;t feel tooooooo much sympathy for the rest of his family, especially when they get on TV and say that until they are given proof they will not accept that he is responsible...even though Rader has confessed.  I am sorry it just really makes me mad!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9785-->
<!--Post: 9801--><!--Time: 1109645892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9801"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 6:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I completely understand how you feel.  However, we have to think about it as if it happened to someone in our family - I would certainly be full of disbelief and stand by my husband until truth prevailed.  Look at Scott Peterson&#39;s family - they are still staunch believers of his and he was tried and convicted of murdering his wife and unborn son.   <BR> <BR>Unless it comes out that his wife knew about his crimes early on and kept quiet, I have nothing but compassion for her at this point in the game.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9801-->
<!--Post: 9804--><!--Time: 1109646205-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9804"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 7:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As a follow-up, I do want to say that I saw an interview with the two surviving Otero children &#40;now adults&#41; and my heart broke.  Hearing Charlie Otero talk about finding the bodies of his family made me so sad.  He was never given a chance to lead a normal life after that - how could he?  And he looks so much like his father and she looks so much like the mother.  It&#39;s all so senseless!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9804-->
<!--Post: 9830--><!--Time: 1109656757-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9830"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 9:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The bottom line is that crime is an ugly thing. <BR> <BR>Tornado, very well put. I feel the same way. Certainly Rader&#39;s kids are victims but if one must compare levels of suffering, the pain to the families of BTK&#39;s murder victims is far worse than BTK&#39;s actual family. I hope that as time passes, Rader&#39;s wife may say something but I&#39;m not holding my breath. I realize &#34;I never had a clue!&#34; is usually what the spouse will say and maybe it&#39;s accurate but once in a while I wonder.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9830-->
<!--Post: 9880--><!--Time: 1109685851-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9880"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Zenith<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Zenith<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 6:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sometimes we tend to want to compare things too much. I was taught long ago from a music teacher that there doesn&#39;t have to be a &#34;better&#34; or &#34;worse&#34; in everything. Who is the best piano player? Neither, they are different and both excellent.  <BR> <BR>Who is suffering most? Everyone.  <BR> <BR>BTK&#39;s family is suffering terribly, they are the newest victims. Imagine loving your father and finding out he is a murderer. Imagine loving your husband and finding out he kills women and children. KAKE reports his 29 year old son is on suicide watch. BTK&#39;s elderly and frail mother was in the hospital at the time of his arrest. Imagine an elderly mother&#39;s nightmare of finding out her caring son is a monster. She will die living through all this. The family is not only dealing with this immediate shock, their lives will be disrupted more than we can ever imagine. <BR> <BR>His wife will never be able to live in that home again, and she&#39;s near retirement age. The media will continue to swarm them. Everyone will talk about them and whisper and point at them forever. His children if unmarried, imagine meeting potential mates and introducing them to your family. If married, imagine raising or being the grandchildren of BTK. What a horrible legacy. <BR> <BR>And they will have to endure the upcoming trial and media where more of BTK&#39;s horrendous deeds will be shown in detail for all the world to see. I cannot even imagine how they will go on. They are in a sense being slowly murdered themselves, and they&#39;ve done nothing wrong, neither did the murder victims or their families. <BR> <BR>I simply feel sorry for everyone, including all of us.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9880-->
<!--Post: 10186--><!--Time: 1109801008-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10186"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cyndi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cyndi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 2:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very well put Zenith.  Even in custody he continues to hurt and torture people.  People that loved and trusted him.  It&#39;s just a tragedy all around.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10186-->
</table></td></tr></table>
